# The Weekly Challenge 397 - Lubos Kolouch

Solutions for Task 1 (Absent Smallest Positive) and Task 2 (Binary Reflection) in Perl and Python.

## Task 1: Absent Smallest Positive
- Given an array of integers, calculate the arithmetic mean.
- Find the smallest positive integer ($k \ge 1$) that is strictly greater than the average and does not appear in the input array.
- Implemented using set lookups in $O(N)$ time and $O(N)$ space in Perl and Python.

## Task 2: Binary Reflection
- Sort an array in ascending order based on the binary reflection of each element.
- The binary reflection reverses the bit representation without leading zeros and parses back to decimal.
- Ties are broken by original value in ascending order.
- Implemented via Schwartzian transform / key sorting in $O(N \log N)$ time in Perl and Python.
